# Windshift

Use `ws` to manage work in **{{.Workspace.Key}}** ({{.Workspace.Name}}).

> Generated by `ws {{.CLIVersion}}` at {{.GeneratedAt}}. Refresh after CLI or
> workspace workflow changes with `ws config docs`.

## Working rules

- Follow user and repository instructions before this guide.
- When work refers to an item, read it before acting: `ws task get <KEY-123>`.
- Use item keys exactly as returned by `ws`; never construct a key from a
  numeric ID.
- Keep the item status accurate. Move it to an in-progress status when work
  starts and to a completed status only after the requested outcome is done.
- Record durable decisions, blockers, and completion evidence as item comments.
- Use `ws <command> --help` for operations not listed here.

## Direct API access

Use the authenticated API escape hatch only when the normal CLI commands do
not expose an operation. OpenAPI paths default to `/rest/api/v2`; the response
body is printed unchanged.

```bash
ws api /items/<item-id>/history
ws api /items/<item-id> -X PATCH -H 'If-Match: "etag"' -d '{"title":"New"}'
ws api /items/bulk-update -X POST --input payload.json
ws api /openapi.json                       # Discover available v2 routes
```

Use `ws api --help` for stdin, response-header, and full-path syntax.

## Work items

```bash
ws task mine                              # Items assigned to me
ws task created                           # Items I created
ws task get <KEY-123>                     # Details, parent, children, comments
ws task create -t "Title" [-d "Details"]
ws task edit <KEY-123> [-t "Title"] [-d "Details"] [--assignee <user-id>]
ws task move <KEY-123> <status>           # Change status
ws task parent <KEY-123>
ws task children <KEY-123>
ws comment list <KEY-123>
ws comment add <KEY-123> -m "Markdown body"
ws link ls <KEY-123>                      # Linked items, pages, and tests
```

Include the item key in commit subjects when the commit belongs to tracked
work, for example: `fix: handle empty input ({{.Workspace.Key}}-123)`.

## Attachments

Attach screenshots, logs, or generated files to an item rather than pasting
them into a comment.

```bash
ws attachment upload <KEY-123> shot.png [more.png ...]  # Attach local files
ws attachment list <KEY-123>                            # Attachment IDs and sizes
ws attachment download <attachment-id> [--to <path>]    # Fetch one back
```

