## Documentation

Search documentation before guessing at requirements. Search results contain
page metadata; fetch the selected page to read its Markdown body.

```bash
ws page search "keyword or phrase" [--limit 20]  # Search titles and content
ws page list [--label spec]                       # Browse visible pages
ws page get <page-id>                             # Read page Markdown
ws link ls page:<page-id>                         # Find linked work items
```

Follow repository documentation policy. If no more specific policy exists,
use Windshift Pages for durable shared documentation:

```bash
ws page create --title "Title" --file document.md
ws page edit <page-id> --file document.md
ws link add <KEY-123> page:<page-id>
ws page labels <page-id> [--add <label-id>] [--remove <label-id>]
```

## Workspace skills

Skills contain additional workspace-specific instructions. Load a skill only
when its name and description match the current task.

```bash
ws skill ls
ws skill get <skill-id>
```

## Test management

Use these only when the work item or repository workflow uses Windshift test
runs:

```bash
ws test case ls
ws test run mine
ws test run get <run-id>
ws test result <run-id> <case-id> passed|failed|blocked|skipped
```
